TERMS

This program and its source are SyMoNeuRaL's own work. No permission is granted to copy,
distribute, modify or create derivative works from it, and no licence is granted by
implication or estoppel. It is published here only in the sense that it lives in this
repository; the repository has no git remote and its history has never left the machine it
was written on.

If that changes, read "What is SyMoNeuRaL's, and must never be published" in
.claude/CLAUDE.md before anything is pushed.

PROVENANCE -- WHY THIS FILE CAN SAY "ALL RIGHTS RESERVED" AT ALL

A proprietary notice on a file containing somebody else's code is a false statement, so the
claim above is only worth making if it is checked. Every line of desktop-client/ was written
for this repository. Nothing was copied in from an upstream project, a template, a scaffold
generator or a tutorial: the Tauri scaffold here is hand-written, which is also why there is
no package.json, no lockfile from a generator, no node_modules and no bundler. `references/`
was not drawn on -- that directory is reference-only, and using code from it would require a
rebrand first.

THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES

The program links against third-party code that it does not include and does not relicense.
Two groups, with different obligations, and they are worth keeping apart.

1. Rust crates, compiled in.
   433 packages in the dependency graph, licences read from `cargo metadata` on 2026-08-21
   rather than assumed:

       203  MIT OR Apache-2.0            17  Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT
        99  MIT                           9  Unlicense OR MIT
        32  Apache-2.0 OR MIT             5  MPL-2.0
        19  MIT/Apache-2.0                4  BSD-3-Clause (2 dual with MIT/Apache-2.0)
        18  Unicode-3.0                   remainder dual-licensed permissive

   There is no GPL-licensed crate in the graph. Five are MPL-2.0 -- cssparser,
   cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext and selectors -- which is file-level copyleft:
   the obligation attaches to those files, they are used unmodified, and their source is the
   published upstream. Two crates (r-efi) offer LGPL-2.1-or-later as one option among three;
   the MIT/Apache-2.0 options are taken.

   Their copyright notices are the upstream projects' and are not ours to remove. This notice
   does not claim their work.

2. System libraries, linked dynamically, not redistributed.
   Tauri renders through the WebKitGTK already installed on the machine rather than bundling
   a browser engine -- webkit2gtk-4.1 2.52.5, javascriptcoregtk-4.1 2.52.5, libsoup-3.0
   3.6.5, gtk+-3.0 3.24.49, glib-2.0 2.84.4 on this box. These are LGPL and BSD libraries
   supplied by the operating system. They are not copied into this repository and are not
   shipped by it, so nothing here redistributes them.

   That is the substantive reason for choosing Tauri over Electron, quite apart from size: an
   Electron build would bundle and therefore redistribute a Chromium, which brings a much
   larger third-party corpus into the artefact this notice covers.

WHAT THIS PROGRAM IS NOT

It contains no model weights, no training data and no part of the method that produces them.
It does not read training/corpus.jsonl or training/build_dataset.py, and it must not be made
to: those are the protected artefacts, and they are protected only by not being public.

The client talks to the API and renders what the API returns. Publish the numbers, keep the
methods.
